  "body": "**Replaces #399**, which was opened from the old fork. GitHub detached that fork from this repo's network when NeoTech/Camcraft was briefly private, so it can no longer be updated. This branch carries the merges with main through #461, including #381, #395 and #431, and #348's tool-library commits, since #348 was closed unmerged.\n\n**Stacked on #381** (tool bodies: `SetToolBody`, the envelope) **and #348** (tool library buttons in the same editor page). This diff includes both until they merge; the #371 work is e0219f1. Part of #361.\n\n## What changed\n**Tool editor: a \"Tool body\" column.**\n- **Import body…** (STEP/STL/OBJ through the app's importer) and **Clear body**.\n- Placement controls: an axis combo (±X/±Y/±Z of the model, or a picked direction), **Tip offset**, and **Pick tip** / **Pick axis** toggles.\n- A small 3D preview: egui-painted, drag to orbit, no GPU.\n- A live placement note (\"placed: foot … to top …\" or the reason it won't place), and **Apply body**.\n- The 2D profile preview draws the placed body's revolved envelope in amber over the cylinders.\n- A tool not yet in the document shows \"Add the tool first…\".\n\n**Picking.** A click casts a ray through `tool_body_view::pick`.\n- **Pick tip** snaps to the nearest corner of the hit facet and sets the offset so that corner is the tip.\n- **Pick axis** takes the clicked facet's outward normal.\n- Picks only fill the fields; they never queue a command.\n\n**Commands.**\n- **Apply body** queues one `SetToolBody`, a single undo step. **Clear body** is the same command with `None`.\n- Refusals show in the editor by name (\"tool body not set: …\", \"tool body not imported: …\") and the draft is kept.\n- The draft reloads only when the world's body changes (Apply / Undo / Redo / Open), so an unapplied import survives other edits.\n\n**Simulation.** While the transport runs, the running tool's body is posed at the playhead (read from the cached timeline) and drawn as a shaded, depth-tested part. A tool without a body draws exactly as before.\n\n**App-layer helpers**, so ui stays thin: `crates/app/src/tool_body_view.rs` holds `load`, `preview` (the same place-and-envelope step as the command, uncommitted), `pick`, `tip_offset_at`, `posed` and `body_for_operation`.\n\n`docs/decisions/371-tool-body-ui.md` records why picking lives in the editor's own preview rather than the main viewport. Among other reasons, a pick mode there would compete with the face/edge/vertex picks.\n\n## How tested\n- New app `tool_body_view` (6 tests). `tool_body` (8) still passes.\n- 6 new structural UI tests (`egui_app/tests/tool_body.rs`):\n  - the editor offers Import/Clear;\n  - Apply lands one `SetToolBody`, with Undo/Redo and Clear plus its undo;\n  - a degenerate placement is refused by name;\n  - a tip pick fills the offset and queues nothing;\n  - a missing file is refused by name;\n  - the sim draws the body at the playhead, and nothing without one.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib`: 307 passed. `--test operations`: 31/31. `clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --tests -D warnings`: clean.\n- **Expected failure: the pixel snapshot `tool_editor_snapshot`.** The editor is wider (third column) and anchored further left, so its pixels changed. The PNG is deliberately **not** regenerated: #359 (#255) moves pixel goldens to the release lane, after which this test runs and is refreshed only at the cut. The headless-GPU tests also fail here (no adapter on this Mac), the same as on main.\n\n## Not exercised (draft until the contributor tries a build)\n- Hands-on GUI check: the import, picking, apply/undo and simulation flow, on a release build.\n- The body file is read on the UI thread, so a very large vendor STEP freezes the window briefly while loading.\n- Not in this slice: lathe-body placement UI (#369's frame), turning the body about its axis for display, and drawing a body outside the simulation.\n\nChangelog: The tool editor imports a holder body (STEP/STL/OBJ), places it by picking its tip and axis, and the simulation draws the real holder (#371)\n\nFixes #371\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
